@page "/docs"
<PageTitle>Documentation — Kodon</PageTitle>
<PageHeader />
<section class="inner-page section-wrap docs-page"><div class="eyebrow">DOCUMENTATION</div><h1>Build your way with <em>Kodon.</em></h1><p class="page-lede">A practical guide to your workspace, agents, context, and usage.</p><div class="docs-layout"><aside><a class="active" href="#getting-started">Getting started</a><a href="#agents">Working with agents</a><a href="#context">Connecting context</a><a href="#billing">Usage and billing</a></aside><div><article id="getting-started"><span class="doc-number">01</span><h2>Getting started</h2><p>Create a workspace, describe the outcome you want, and invite Kodon to help. The clearer the goal, the more useful the first draft.</p><p>For the best result, include the audience, deadline, source material, and what a successful answer should look like.</p></article><article id="agents"><span class="doc-number">02</span><h2>Working with agents</h2><p>Choose a specialized agent or let Kodon route the work. You can review progress, redirect the approach, or take over at any point.</p><p>Use research agents for discovery, drafting agents for first versions, and review agents for checking structure, accuracy, and tone.</p></article><article id="context"><span class="doc-number">03</span><h2>Connecting context</h2><p>Bring the files and instructions your agent needs into the workspace. Your context stays organized and available when it matters.</p></article><article id="billing"><span class="doc-number">04</span><h2>Usage and billing</h2><p>Credits are consumed when agents complete work. Monitor your balance in the dashboard and add a $10, $20, or $50 pack whenever your project needs more capacity.</p></article></div></div></section>
